{
  "id": "99d19246-1ba9-4720-9895-e70c66acf144",
  "featureId": "ebb9ceb0-ea12-4374-af6e-12aa4256bcc3",
  "number": 67,
  "shortId": "73GZ3",
  "priority": 11,
  "slug": "plugin-ui-declarative-widget-tree-ui-model-viewnode",
  "title": "plugin-ui: Declarative widget-tree UI model (ViewNode)",
  "discussedAt": "",
  "contextReady": false,
  "contextReadyReason": "",
  "summary": "The serializable widget tree plugins author, SwiftUI/Flutter-style — a container node holds a vector of child widgets — plus the host mapper that realizes it into the retained heca-grid-ui tree. Gate/consumers: the rich overlay body (plugin-task-15), config-plugin render (plugin-task-21), and the WASM contribution description (plugin-task-26) all build on this. Source: docs/chrome-and-ui.md §2.6.1–2.6.2.",
  "description": "ViewNode { kind, props, events, children } + PropValue + Intent, all serde-serializable (WASM-ready). WidgetKind covers the WHOLE grid-ui vocabulary. Behaviour is Intent-only (no closures) so it stays serializable for native AND plugin/WASM. Includes the surface compositor + LayerRegistry (layered-surface architecture for KeyHint visibility) and the OverlayHost (open_modal/resolve).",
  "notes": "",
