  "updatedAt": "2026-07-28T06:45:55.036Z",
  "handoff": "# Session handoff — 2026-07-27 → 28\n\n**Reason:** context spent. Everything committed and pushed; tree clean; **985 tests, clippy 0\nwarnings**. Nothing half-built.\n\n## Read this first: how this user works\n\nTwo rounds of real frustration today, both earned. Read this before writing code.\n\n- **Nothing hardcoded that is data.** The day's recurring defect: solved for the one case in front of\n  the author, wrong the moment the model is used as designed. Three found in one session — the focus\n  key naming a *side*, a scroll offset keyed by container *kind*, a shell owning a scroll area that\n  belongs to whoever nests one.\n- **The model, in their words:** a **widget** is a component like React's, placeable anywhere, holding\n  its own logic — move it around the app and it behaves the same, no reinvention. A **container** holds\n  widgets and may nest a scroll area. A **sidebar** is a shell hosting containers, knowing almost\n  nothing about them. **Left/right is only position.** Placing a container twice is *placing it twice*.\n- **Reuse what exists; invent nothing.** `flex_grow` already was the fractional share; `Glyph::ALL`\n  already existed; the resize *mode* already existed; `ResizeAxis` already covers x/y. Every time I\n  proposed machinery they asked whether something already did it, and it usually did. **Search first.**\n- **They verify anything visual themselves.** Green tests never verify layout or interaction.\n- **Assert what was reported.** A test asserting a `grow` *flag* passed while the layout was visibly\n  broken; the measured-height test caught it. If a bug was visible, measure the visible thing.\n- **Never decide whether a task lives or dies**, and do not act on an instruction's letter when the next\n  step needs otherwise — ask. **\"We are discussing\" means stop writing.**\n- **Commit messages say what changed.** Prior-error archaeology belongs in the task.\n- **`git checkout <file>` destroyed uncommitted work twice.** Copy to the scratchpad first. A global\n  find-and-replace also broke code outside its intent — bound every edit.\n\n## Where the work is\n\nBranch `feat/action-arg-declaration`, pushed. **PR #250** —\nhttps://github.com/ovidius72/heca/pull/250 (PR #249 merged; #250 is everything after it).\n\n## Closed this session\n\nF003/P011 **T006** (typed builder SDK — the user confirmed the described and native panels are\nidentical), **T018** (`PropValue::Map`, so `border`/`glow` are authorable at last), **T019** (fixed\nvalue sets as types), plus all of T021's implementation.\n\nCommits: `f2deecd` `1653169` `7183250` `189a2cd` `096f06e` `1f4b92d` `7b3a624` `fd403dd` `1d75cb3`\n`3084714` `8c65a54` `c65ae90` `fcbba56` `95a894d`.\n\n**The technical lesson worth carrying:** `flex_grow` alone does **not** divide a region — it\ndistributes only *positive* free space, and container content is taller than a sidebar, so two\ncontainers measured **1214px each inside a 600px body**. A share needs a **zero base size + permission\nto shrink** (CSS `flex: 1 1 0`). Then **296px each**, measured. `Layout` has no `flex_basis`, so that\nzero is written as a height today — **do not copy it**; F004/P006/T010 replaces it with one `share(n)`.\n\n## ✅ The test bed is gone and STAYS gone\n\n`95a894d` removed the two extra placements from `heca/src/app/startup.rs`; the right sidebar is empty\nuntil it gets real features. I asked whether to restore it for verifying T012/T020 — **the user said no\n(2026-07-28). Do not re-add it.**\n\nConsequence to plan around: there is **one** container on screen, so focus and \"the focused area\nscrolls, the others decline\" cannot be demonstrated with two real docks. Verify what one container can\nshow, and say plainly what a single container cannot prove rather than quietly asserting it works. A\nsecond real dock is a future feature, not scaffolding to invent.\n\n## Open, in order\n\n1. **T021 — close it.** All implementation and docs are done (`fcbba56`: `docs/widgets.md` + README\n   carry container shares, nested scrolling and the model). The test-bed question is settled above.\n2. **T020 — `FocusDock`.** Chrome keyboard focus as a **container id**, via `ActionRegistry` +\n   `KeymapRegistry` + `KeyHint` (the user's design). One action, two doors: bare → pick a dock by\n   letter; `focus_dock(dock=\"…\")` → direct, for RPC. **Focus must be visible.** Fixes a live bug: the\n   focus key expands the *left* container even when the dock is seated right, which the dock allows.\n3. **T012 — keyboard scrolling (blocked on T020).** Widget half shipped (`096f06e`): eight semantic\n   `WidgetIntent::Scroll*`, `ScrollRegion` owning the paging and the clamp, declining any axis it cannot\n   scroll, `keyboard_target(Signal<bool>)` gating which instance responds. **Route settled 2026-07-28\n   after checking the code:** the bindings are prefix-gated (`prefix+[Shift+]PageUp/PageDown/Home/End`\n   — settled, do not reopen), so they arrive on the `WmAction` path by construction. The widget-keymap\n   idea is **ruled out**: `[keys.widgets]` is consulted at `heca/src/app/events.rs:156` only when a\n   modal is open and the mode is not Prefix. Four actions with an axis argument (reuse `ResizeAxis`),\n   full Adding-New-Actions checklist, handler dispatches `Event::Widget` into the chrome tree.\n4. **F004/P005/T007 — resize handle + resize mode.** Config keeps declaring **fixed** amounts (nothing\n   a user wrote breaks); the **proportion is computed internally per target**; one conversion shared by\n   drag and key; both axes; defaults shipped and customizable. The app hand-rolls divider resizing in\n   `heca/src/mouse/resize.rs` — absorb or delete it, never both.\n5. **F004/P006/T010 — `flex_basis` + one `share(n)` setter**, so no caller writes a fixed measure to\n   express a proportion.\n\n## Facts worth not rediscovering\n\n- `.planner/HANDOFF.md` is **deprecated**; handoffs live on `phase.handoff`.\n- `resume.json`'s `nextSteps`/`notes` are free text that task operations never refresh, and have\n  misdirected two sessions. **Read the task.**\n- `planner-task-show` / `planner-phase-update` can exceed the tool output limit; the response is saved\n  to a file, and `phase-update` **applies** even when it cannot be displayed.\n- Phase status is derived from tasks, so a phase JSON keeps `status: null` while the tool reports done.\n- **Check task statuses against the commits before trusting a recap** — two finished tasks sat\n  `in-progress` for a whole session here.",
